+1 on keeping the three checks separate — and it's already scoping that way: the current recipe is check 1 (body ↔ hash); the witness sig + timestamp and the issuer sig + key-history are checks 2 and 3 — exactly the tiers Fede flagged as follow-ups (they need a schnorr/secp256k1 lib the repo doesn't carry yet). Three recipes, each independently attributable — no bundling guarantees that should stay separable. The evidence-to-verdict derivation you mention sits a layer above that, and it's the interesting one.

@Jimmy — agreed, let's push the integration. The lens + trustless-ai.eth.limo are the concrete things to put in front of their team: not a pitch, a working, self-verifying artifact they  can run. A recomputable pre-action verdict their adjudicators can re-check themselves is the clean seam into Layer 6. Moving forward 🔺

Morning all, serious respect, Fede, that’s a marathon 🙏 (8275 #3, 8323 #4 + the full testkit green, and the independent 8299 recompute check — clean).

@Fede on the registerWithSource overloads, yep, that’s my AgentIdentityRegistry. Here are all three so you can bind the other two precisely, no guessing:

// all: external payable whenNotPaused → returns (uint256 agentId)
// guard on every one: require(msg.value == mintPrice)
//                      require(IERC721(boundCollection).ownerOf(sourceTokenId) == msg.sender)

function registerWithSource(uint256 sourceTokenId);                    // ← the one you bound (uses baseAgentURI template)

function registerWithSource(string calldata agentURI, uint256 sourceTokenId);   // custom agentURI

function registerWithSource(
    string calldata agentURI,
    uint256 sourceTokenId,
    MetadataEntry[] calldata metadata
);                                                                      // custom URI + initial metadata entries

struct MetadataEntry { string metadataKey; bytes metadataValue; }

Semantics: #1 uses the registry’s baseAgentURI template, #2 overrides the URI, #3 also seeds metadata at registration. Live instance to bind/verify against: [REDACTED_WALLET] (mainnet). The kit repo is in final review before going public — I’ll drop the link here the moment it’s up so you can pull the full source rather than a paste.

On the missing-interfaces list: our side’s covered — 8275 + 8323 are yours, and 8299 (WYRIWE) is already in the SDK and you validated it green. The rest (8312, 8294, 8263) sit on their own author lines, so I’ll leave those to them rather than write interfaces for specs I’m not on.

On 8281 (OCP) — I’m the merged external contributor on that one (the L3/L4 inference-attestation appendix), so I’m happy to draft its interface to unblock the SDK, with Damon’s sign-off whenever suits him

Following up on the OCP interface, drafted it, wanted your eyes before I push since it’s your spec, Damon.

IObservationCommitment (ERC-8281), pulled from the spec (#1788) + your reference ObservationCommitment:

// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

/// @title IObservationCommitment — On-chain Commitment Anchor (ERC-8281)
interface IObservationCommitment {
    event Recorded(bytes32 indexed digest, address indexed committer);
    function record(bytes32 digest) external;
}

Kept it to the base v1.0 surface — one write, one event, no getter (verification stays off-chain / recompute-based, the log is the ledger). ERC-165 id recomputes to 0xb5c645bd. README follows the same shape as the ERC8299 folder (spec link, interface table, architecture, reference impl at 0x0963…ED5c Base Sepolia, related ERCs). Attribution: Damon as author, me as interface contributor.

Left the v1.1 Revocation / v1.2 Temporal Bounds extensions out of the base interface — those read like separate contracts / separate interface files if/when you want them in.

Two checks before I open the PR:

@Damon — does this match your intent? One naming thing: spec says the event is Recorded(bytes32 digest, address committer), but the live anchor emits recorder. I followed the spec (committer) — shout if the live one is canonical and I’ll flip it.
@Jimmy / @Fede — is contracts/verify/ERC8281/ the right home, or would you file OCP under a different category?
Once you’re all good I’ll push + open the PR is already staged

